  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760037,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1917: A Revolutionary Comedy for Commodore 64\n\nStep back in time to 1917 in *1917*, a quirky and humorous game for the Commodore 64! Assume the role of a revolutionary leader determined to overthrow a corrupt aristocracy and restore justice to the land. This isn't a serious historical simulation; instead, prepare for a lighthearted, comedic adventure filled with silly situations and charmingly absurd characters.\n\nYour mission: infiltrate the opulent palace of the wealthy elite and confront them in a final, decisive showdown. Navigate through increasingly challenging rooms, dodging guards and overcoming comical obstacles. The game’s short, evocative tune perfectly complements the aesthetic, evoking the feel of a silent movie era. \n\n*1917* offers simple, accessible gameplay, making it enjoyable for players of all skill levels. Expect a focus on comedic timing and unexpected twists as you strive to right the wrongs of the ruling class.  It's a brief but memorable experience, perfect for a quick dose of revolutionary fun with a distinctly playful tone."
    },
